    <p class="section-label">About</p>
    <h2 style="margin-top:0;">Hi, I'm Phil.</h2>
    <p>
      I'm a Product Manager for SCREEn at LMI, working on Pentagon-facing supply chain risk
      management tooling. Before this, I spent 11 years at Boeing, most recently as Senior
      Manager for Third Party Risk &amp; Resilience — building and running programs that help
      a massive organization understand and manage risk in its supplier base.
    </p>
    <p>
      I'm a builder and problem-solver at heart. I'm currently deep in the transition from
      "risk subject-matter expert" to "product manager," which means learning a lot about
      product craft, customer discovery, and shipping software — in public, mostly, right here.
    </p>

    <h2>What I write about</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>Supply chain risk management as a discipline — frameworks, mental models, lessons learned</li>
      <li>Learning product management as a second career, in the open</li>
      <li>Working on Pentagon-facing / government-adjacent programs</li>
      <li>Notes on tools, systems, and how I stay organized</li>
    </ul>
    <p style="font-size:14px;color:var(--ink-mute);">
      A note on scope: I don't write about specific employers, programs, or anything
      confidential — just the craft, principles, and things I've learned that are useful
      more broadly.
    </p>

